    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a very strong position to take. You mentioned an \"inherent nature\" that makes them more prone to deference. Could you expand on that? If we look at the different castes and groups across the subcontinent, do you find that certain types are more suited for specific roles under British rule, or is this lack of \"systematic progress\" something you see across all the various ethnicities and groups in India?",
