      "content": "The inherent differences are quite pronounced, though one must be pragmatic about utility. Certain groups, those with a history of administrative aptitude or a willingness to adopt our methods, are naturally better suited for lower bureaucratic roles. However, the general populace, across most castes, exhibits a fundamental lack of the necessary drive for true, self-directed advancement. It is not merely a matter of caste; it is a pervasive cultural inertia that requires firm, British direction to overcome.",
